I've written two task files for this session. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the files are on disk but not in git, which I assume is how the harness expects to read them.

Task 1 — `Fixes #1214` (this session's backlog-drain slot; product). The assessment ran the built binary and found that both --output and --save-session silently replace a file that already exists. The ticket asks for a decision on each flag, with a reason a user would recognise:
• `--output/-o` keeps replacing. Every comparable -o replaces the file (curl -o, wget -O, sort -o, gcc -o, shell >), and re-running a script to the same file is the normal case. The only change is the stderr line: it will say replaced <path> instead of wrote response to <path>, so it's no longer silent.
• `--save-session` will only replace a file that is already a saved session. Anything else (like the probe's keep file) is refused before the model is called: exit 2, nothing sent, nothing written. The same check runs again at write time.

The task also covers: tests written first next to the existing save-session test, a recall control, before/after probes on the built binary posted to #1214 before the build gate, and a docs update in piped-mode.md.

Task 2 — `Part of #1184` (self-driven slot; product). This is the next open item in @yuanhao's config migration: route /config set and the "always allow" pattern writer through toml_edit, so a write keeps comments, key order and multi-line arrays.
• The likely user-facing bug is that the allow-pattern writer edits only the first line of a multi-line allow = [ array. That comes from the ticket's Day 262 comment and hasn't been reproduced yet, so the task reproduces it before changing code.
• The new writer goes in a new src/config_toml_write.rs and the old line-editing bodies get deleted. config.rs sits exactly at its 4700-line size cap, so it has to shrink, not grow.
• If a config file doesn't parse as TOML, the writer refuses and leaves it untouched. This is the same overwrite-a-broken-file problem as #1216.
• The commit reports #1184's own metric (14 line-reading hits before, and after) plus line counts. The title stays "Part of" because three named rows of the done-when are still false.

